  "material": {
    "about": "Glass: one material in three levels (dashboard/DESIGN.md › Material). bar: the site's header past 8 px, the app's window band, sticky toolbars. panel: menus, popovers, tooltips, toasts, floating pills. card: a card over a calm art ground only, never over imagery or logos. art: a small piece directly on brand art (the prompt pill on a card's art), the same in both appearances, with its own edge, highlight and solid fallback. edge-hover and card-hover are a linked glass card's hover (Card variant glass). Each level falls back to its solid surface without backdrop-filter or with reduced transparency. Budget: blur at most 24 px and at most 12 glass layers on screen (16 Oct 2026, Chrome at 120 Hz: p95 frame 9.2 ms with or without glass at 20 to 24 px; 40 px dropped frames).",
    "glass": {
      "bar": { "light": "paper 78%", "dark": "paper 72%", "blur": 20, "saturate": 160 },
      "panel": { "light": "#FFFFFF 72%", "dark": "#1E1E1E 70%", "blur": 24, "saturate": 180 },
      "card": { "light": "#FFFFFF 60%", "dark": "#1E1E1E 60%", "blur": 20, "saturate": 150 },
      "art": { "light": "#FFFFFF 10%", "dark": "#FFFFFF 10%", "edge": "#FFFFFF 14%", "highlight": "#FFFFFF 34%", "fallback": "#121212 72%", "blur": 16, "saturate": 140 }
    },
    "edge": { "light": "#000000 8%", "dark": "#FFFFFF 9%" },
    "highlight": { "light": "#FFFFFF 60%", "dark": "#FFFFFF 14%" },
    "edge-hover": { "light": "#000000 13%", "dark": "#FFFFFF 16%" },
    "card-hover": { "light": "#FFFFFF 60%", "dark": "#FFFFFF 3%" }
  },
  "ui": {
    "about": "The names the Mac app's stylesheets read (dashboard/src/index.css, components/ui/ui.css), generated into the app and mobster.dev by scripts/gen_brand_tokens.py as brand:tokens as=ui regions, so a primitive styled once reads the same on both. type: size and line height in px; hero is a screen that is the whole window (the first run, the plan, sign-in) at desktop widths, the display ramp's first step as on Remote's pages, and no page in the app's frame uses it. control: heights in px; xl is mobster.dev's landing actions only, the app never uses it. row: a list row's least height in px, by what it holds: item, one line in a menu, picker or palette; list, one line with its mark in a page's list (ListRow); detail, a title over a line (a settings row, a conversation). radius: px; app-icon is a proportion; xl is mobster.dev's cards only, the app never uses it. alpha and alias are per appearance; semantic is the same in both and reads the per-appearance names.",
